{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":233896,"name":"colin h winter","username":"markovianprotocol","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar/markovianprotocol/{size}/5_341fea102a12413267ee9cca6a635b61.png","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:34:13.221Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThe answer above (post 23) says “critical vulnerabilities are released within 24 hours”, across every supported release. Since June, 57 kernel CVEs in ubuntu-cve-tracker were raised from medium to critical on their Ubuntu CVSS v4 score (“Priority reason: See ubuntu cvss score”). Of the 24 fixed after being raised, none was fixed within a week, at a median of 16.5 days; 9 more were still waiting on 20 October. The tracker commit, fix date and release status for each one, with the scripts: \u003ca href=\"https://markovianprotocol.com/measurements/sm-023.html?r=ubuntufaq\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://markovianprotocol.com/measurements/sm-023.html?r=ubuntufaq\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThree questions, which we’ll print with your answers: does the 24-hour line cover kernel CVEs raised to critical from the CVSS score, and if not, will the FAQ or the label change? Under the two-week kernel cycle announced on 23 September, what should users expect for those? And for the 14 that are fixed on some supported releases but still needed on others, is there a date?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-10-21T04:26:51.592Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":89999,"topic_slug":"question-for-publication","display_username":"colin h winter","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://markovianprotocol.com/measu